<h2>What the guarantee covers</h2>
<p>Reviews are easier to judge when you know the promise behind them. Our <a href="/ticket-buyer-protection">ticket buyer protection page</a> says orders are covered for valid tickets, delivery before the event, secure payment processing and customer support if something goes wrong. If there is a problem with the validity of your tickets, we work to provide replacement tickets of equal or better value or a full refund. If an event is canceled and not rescheduled, you receive a full refund.</p>
<p>You can read the full terms on our <a href="/worry-free-guarantee">worry-free guarantee page</a>. Event-specific rules, such as refunds for postponed shows, can differ, so check the event page and our <a href="/ticket-faq">ticket FAQ</a> before you buy.</p>
<div class="so-callout">
  <p><strong>A note on prices:</strong> Seat Outlet is a resale marketplace. Ticket prices are set by sellers and may be above or below face value, so compare seats before you check out.</p>
</div>

<h2>Where to go next</h2>
<p>If you are still deciding, the quickest check is to look at an event you care about, compare seats and read the policies. Our guide on <a href="/how-to-buy-tickets-online">how to buy tickets online</a> walks through each step, and you can browse by category with the links on the <a href="/buy-tickets-online">buy tickets online page</a>. For more about the company, see <a href="/about-seat-outlet">about Seat Outlet</a>.</p>

